e to take more responsibility for its own security.", "published_at": "2026-09-01T12:01:49+00:00", "image_url": "https://www.politico.eu/cdn-cgi/image/width=1200,height=630,fit=crop,quality=80,onerror=redirect/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/01/GettyImages-2286752296-scaled.jpg", "source": {"name": "Politico Europe", "tier": "international", "url": "https://www.politico.eu"}, "bias_scores": [{"political_lean": 50, "sensationalism": 10, "opinion_fact": 25, "factual_rigor": 50, "framing": 14, "confidence": 0.7, "rationale": {"framing": {"connotation_score": 8.3, "keyword_emphasis_score": 0.0, "omission_score": 39.2, "headline_body_divergence": 23.7, "has_cluster_context": true}}}]}}, {"article": {"id": "fa9b79a3-5071-45f6-af13-c6fcfc89a8cf", "title": "Radu Miruta attends EU defence ministers' Wicklow meeting; maritime security discussed", "url": "https://actmedia.eu/daily/radu-miruta-attends-eu-defence-ministers-wicklow-meeting-maritime-security-discussed/121475", "summary": "&nbsp;EU defence ministers, meeting Monday and Tuesday in Wicklow, Ireland, discussed the Union's support for Ukraine, the role of outer space in security and defence, developments in the Middle East, and maritime security.According to the Romanian Defence Ministry, the exchange of views highlighted the need to strengthen cooperation and Europe's response capacity to threats affecting freedom of navigation, maritime routes and the resilience of strategic infrastructure. Minister Radu Miruta stressed the need for increased vigilance and presented the recent situation in Romania's exclusive economic zone in the Black Sea, along with the measures taken.In the session dedicated to Ukraine, ministers reviewed the latest developments in EU support and the deepening of EU-Ukraine industrial cooperation. Discussions also covered lessons learned from implementing the Ukraine Support Loan on its military component and from mobilising the European Peace Facility.Regarding the EU's contribution...", "published_at